{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Its fat, the entire fat-tail.</b> Its meaning is as it is, that the fat-tail is called fat, and the Sadducees erred, as I shall explain to you in the second portion. Also the Gaon [Saadia] erred, who said that it means \"its fat and the fat-tail,\" for by the precision of the language it is impossible, for it would be proper to be \"its fat and its fat-tail\" or \"the fat and the fat-tail.\"" "<b>The caul.</b> It is known from its place, and it has no cognate, and there are some who derived it from the root עץ in a far-fetched way."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {1 "Ibn Ezra writes אח ('brother/cognate'); I translate 'cognate' per standard grammatical usage. 'From the root עץ' literally means 'from the root of עץ (tree/wood),' apparently a forced etymology."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:08:34.219158628Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}